/**
 * Golden chunk rivers. For three seeds (the third with finite continents), 10 chunks each (one without rivers, then three
 * river chunks from each of three scan windows, negative and positive coordinates): the number of columns with a river, a
 * hash over the 256 {@link RiverInfo}s (the edge's source, drain and width, the flow, and the raw bits of the square distance
 * and width), a hash over the 256 interpolated column flows, a hash of the square distances when each column reads its own
 * partition point instead of the chunk's (TFC's uncached path), and one hash per {@link RiverBlendType} of its sampler over
 * every third column: the height for four input heights and three weights, and the density for y in 40..110 (step 2) with
 * the input densities 0 and 0.7.
 * <p>
 * The values come from TerraFirmaCraft at c3b4d9536 (the pinned commit): an oracle harness compiled TFC's region and river
 * classes and the 3D noise unchanged (with {@code TFCChunkGenerator} stubbed to its sea level), copied TFC's
 * {@code sampleRiverEdge}, {@code sampleRiverData} and {@code calculateFlowAt} with the block position as parameters, and
 * printed these lines with Minecraft 1.21.11's {@code Mth} and {@code XoroshiroRandomSource}. The samplers were created as
 * {@code TFCChunkGenerator.createRiverSamplersForChunk} does: one {@code Seed.of(levelSeed)}, in enum order. 30 golden lines.
 */
